        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Right eye redness and mucopurulent discharge for 3 days, now bilateral with left eye symptoms since yesterday; marked morning crusting; mild eyelid oedema in the morning that improves during the day; grittiness and mild discomfort. Denies significant pain, photophobia, reduced vision, foreign body, trauma, chemical exposure, and contact lens use. Mild upper respiratory infection last week, now resolved. Exposure to children with 'pink eye'."
      }
